```json
[
 {
  "id": "F1",
  "file": "src/evals/trace.ts",
  "line": 71,
  "title": "The trace report can credit trace with a defect the main reviewer already caught",
  "detail": "Candidates with `raisedBy: [1]` are treated as trace additions and matched against gold on their own. When the main reviewer and the trace finder report the same gold defect with titles or scenarios different enough to escape the merge, `addedOnGold` still counts it for trace, although the main report already catches that defect. The issue asks for the trace finder's findings to be reported separately (added, landed on gold, blocked a clean case), and this inflates its gold credit. Count a trace addition as landing on gold only when it matches a required defect that the main finder's own report did not catch (match the main report against gold first, then credit trace only for the remaining defects). Add a test with a main finding and a trace finding on the same gold defect under different titles: trace gets no gold credit."
 }
]
```

